From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meta-flax <meta-flax@tiogapass>
Date: Mon, 07 Apr 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix BIOS activation and failure cleanup in FWUPD_SCRIPT mode

Three bugs fixed:

1. In the FWUPD_SCRIPT activation path, flashWrite() (fwupd@.service,
   looks for image-bmc) is called for all VersionPurpose values.  Add
   an early-return for VersionPurpose::Host that calls flashWriteHost()
   (obmc-flash-host-bios@.service) instead.  Placed before the
   WANT_SIGNATURE_VERIFY and apply-time check blocks so those patches
   continue to apply cleanly.

2. AMI patch 0007 comments out the #ifdef HOST_BIOS_UPGRADE block in
   unitStateChange() that routes BIOS service state changes to
   onStateChangesBios().  Add a duplicate block after the original so
   that 0007 only comments the original, leaving this copy intact and
   preserving the routing.

3. onStateChangesBios() failure path only sets Activations::Failed but
   leaves the D-Bus activation object alive and activationProgress set.
   This blocks all subsequent upload attempts and causes the web UI to
   show "Error in switching running and backup images" until BMC reboot.
   Add cleanup matching the success path: reset activationProgress and
   erase the version object so the web UI recovers immediately.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AMI integration bug]
---
--- a/activation.cpp
+++ b/activation.cpp
@@ -104,6 +104,16 @@
             activationProgress =
                 std::make_unique<ActivationProgress>(bus, path);
 
+#ifdef HOST_BIOS_UPGRADE
+            auto purpose = parent.versions.find(versionId)->second->purpose();
+            if (purpose == VersionPurpose::Host)
+            {
+                activationProgress->progress(20);
+                flashWriteHost();
+                return softwareServer::Activation::activation(value);
+            }
+#endif
+
 #ifdef WANT_SIGNATURE_VERIFY
             fs::path uploadDir(IMG_UPLOAD_DIR);
             if (!verifySignature(uploadDir / versionId, SIGNED_IMAGE_CONF_PATH))
@@ -367,6 +377,19 @@
     }
 #endif
 
+    // AMI patch 0007 comments out the block above; this duplicate ensures
+    // BIOS service state changes are still routed to onStateChangesBios().
+#ifdef HOST_BIOS_UPGRADE
+    {
+        auto purpose = parent.versions.find(versionId)->second->purpose();
+        if (purpose == VersionPurpose::Host)
+        {
+            onStateChangesBios(msg);
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     onStateChanges(msg);
 
     return;
@@ -497,6 +520,12 @@
             activation(softwareServer::Activation::Activations::Failed);
 
             error("Bios upgrade failed.");
+
+            // Clean up so the web UI can recover without a BMC reboot.
+            activationProgress.reset(nullptr);
+            boost::asio::post(getIOContext(), [this]() {
+                this->parent.erase(this->versionId);
+            });
         }
     }
 
